<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saipan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saipan is the largest island and seat of government of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-mariana-islands">Northern Mariana Islands</a>, a US commonwealth in the western Pacific. Under Japanese rule from 1914 it was developed for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> cane with many settlers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and Okinawa. In June and July 1944 US forces captured it in one of the bloodiest battles of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-war">Pacific War</a>, in which thousands of Japanese civilians died, many by suicide, and it became a base for bombing Japan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saipan.jpg" alt="Saipan" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MICHAELeDILLEY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saipan_at_Night.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
